                                 Vim Text Editor
                
--> Text editor is a software tool used to create, view and modify text files.

vi text editor?
--> vi stands for Visual Interface. 
--> it is classssic text editor commanly found on unix system but 
having limited features.

**vim
--> vim stands for Vi IMproved
--> it is advanced version of vi with more advanced features.

** VIM modes:
1. Normal mode:
--> when you open vim, it noremally starts in normal mode
--> you can not type text directly in this mode.
--> it can be accessed from other modes by using 'esc'

2. Insert mode:
--> insert mode allows you to type text or edit text.
--> to enter insert mode use 'i'

3. Command line / command execute mode:
--> this mode allows you to execute commands.
--> type ':' and then enter command

4. Visual mode
--> to enter visual mode use 'v'
--> A mode that provides additional options for selecting text.

**syntax to create or open file:
vim <file_name>
vim demo.txt

**Save and quit commands:
:w and <enter> = to save file
:q and <enter> = to quit file
:q! and <enter> =  to force quit 
:wq and <enter> = to save and exit
:set nu = display line numbers
:set nonu = hide line numbers

*Cursor movement
h = move left
j = move down
k = move up
l = move right
    OR
 arrow keys

 gg = go to first line of the afile
 shift+g = go to last line of the file

*Search and replace
--> Top to bottom
syntax= /word
eg= /AWS

use 'n' for the next occurance of serach word.

--> Bottom to Top
syntax= ?word
eg= ?AWS

--> Replace word
syntax= :%s/word1/word2/g
eg= :%s/AWS/Microsoft Azure/g
--> this command is used to replace the word1 with word2 globally.

